# What the source distribution ships beyond the package itself.
#
# The driving requirement: `pytest` must pass in an unpacked sdist. Without
# this file setuptools shipped tests/ but silently omitted tests/conftest.py,
# so every module importing a shared fixture failed at collection -- 7 errors
# out of the box for anyone building from source. Shipping *some* of a test
# suite is worse than shipping none.

include LICENSE
include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md

# The whole test suite, conftest included.
recursive-include tests *.py

# ...and the fixtures it reads. tests/test_matching_invariance.py compares
# against stored expectations; shipping the test without its data would fail
# in an unpacked sdist, which is the exact failure this file exists to prevent.
recursive-include tests/data *.json

# tests/test_docs.py executes every Python block in the documentation, so the
# docs are a test fixture as well as prose. Markdown only -- the methodology
# figures are large, are not read by any test, and would bloat the sdist.
recursive-include docs *.md

# Everything below is development scaffolding, not part of a source build.
exclude .gitlab-ci.yml
prune .plans
prune .github
prune benchmarks
prune examples
prune docs/figures
prune site
